# Attachment upload hop

| Browser | Body | Transport |
|---|---|---|
| Chrome | one Blob PUT `/file` | `fetch(Blob)` (XHR only if progress) |
| Safari ≤ 6 MiB | one Blob PUT `/file` | XHR, no `upload.*` listeners |
| Safari > 6 MiB | few ~4 MiB serial PUTs `/file/chunks/:i` | XHR, no `upload.*` listeners |

Common: same-site page → `upload[-staging].privatenote.ai`, Bearer then query, `credentials: "omit"`, never Pages `/api` for the binary body.

Safari multi‑MiB single PUT currently aborts in ~200–600 ms (`status: 0`, no `responseURL`) while Chrome succeeds on the same hop — keep Safari chunking on until that delta is fixed (CF/Bot Fight / WebKit).

## CORS (upload relay)

Match `relay.encrypt.lu`: echo Origin, Allow-Headers echo (authorization), Allow-Methods GET/POST/PUT/OPTIONS, Max-Age 86400, **no** Allow-Credentials, **no** Set-Cookie.

## Server

Drain `request.arrayBuffer()` **before** any 4xx/5xx on attachment PUT/POST — early closes become Safari status 0.
